# Every error has the same shape: { statusCode, code, message, requestId } plus safe extras.
# The message is fixed text for the code; it never repeats what was sent.
# There is no public POST route yet, so the body examples use a missing one: Fastify parses the
# body before deciding the route is missing. Real routes get their own files from C8 on.

### Unknown route: 404 not_found, and the path and query are not echoed back
GET {{baseUrl}}/no-such-route?q=anything

### Malformed JSON: 400 invalid_json, with no part of the body in the answer
POST {{baseUrl}}/no-such-route
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "broken

### Empty JSON body: 400 invalid_json
POST {{baseUrl}}/no-such-route
Content-Type: application/json

### A request id you send (UUID only) comes back in X-Request-Id and in the error body
GET {{baseUrl}}/no-such-route
X-Request-Id: 9b2f6c1e-3d4a-4f5b-8c7d-0e1f2a3b4c5d
